POM itself is a pixel shading effect. The separate user-authored WPO raises the demo snow surface by 10 uu on an upward-facing plane.
Neither change modifies collision, RT data, or world window mapping.
When the editor exposes no level viewport, the report keeps that PIE rerun as BLOCKED and identifies any prior same-HLSL capture used for visual evidence.
